WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.830
Every dead character who stays dead in the
MCU is potential money that's slipping through

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.020
Disney's couch cushions.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.460
So when a hero or villain takes a dirt nap,
you can rest assured there was a solid reason

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.960
for it, and possibly one that will have larger
implications down the road.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.580
Many spoilers ahead!

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.340
Remember the Other?

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.899
In The Avengers, this double-thumbed alien
acted as middleman between Thanos and Loki.

00:00:21.899 --> 00:00:27.020
In 2014's Guardians of the Galaxy, he's casually
murdered by an irritated Ronan the Accuser.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:31.090
The madman wants Thanos's attention and is
frankly quite tired of the Titan's emissary

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:31.900
barking at him.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.880
"I only ask that you take this matter seriously."

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.820
No, the Other isn't a major character, though
fans of early Joss Whedon TV shows Buffy the

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.220
Vampire Slayer and Angel were probably a little
disappointed to see him go.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.360
The alien was played by Alexis Denisof, who
played Wesley Wyndham-Pryce, a Buffyverse

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.740
character initially so annoying it's amazing
no one ever broke his neck.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:53.180
"Excuse me."

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.000
In the 2018 prose novel Thanos: The Titan
Consumed by Barry Lyga, we learn that Ronan

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.800
did more than dispatch an annoying intermediary
here.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:07.560
The Other is a Chitauri, specifically the
only Chitauri to be a bona fide individual.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.350
He negotiated Thanos taking over the leadership
of his people.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.970
The rest of the Chitauri share a hive mind,
which is why they all die when their command

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:15.500
ship is destroyed in Avengers.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.460
When Ronan kills The Other, it's really a
bit like finding the Holy Grail and tossing

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.820
it into an active volcano.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.280
Of course, Ronan is also a psychotic maniac.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.680
"He chose… poorly."

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:32.940
When Quicksilver was killed by Ultron in Avengers:
Age of Ultron, it was natural for many viewers

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:37.031
to assume the choice was made to forestall
any confusion between the MCU Quicksilver

00:01:37.031 --> 00:01:41.299
played by Aaron Taylor-Johnson and the version
of the character introduced in Fox's X-Men:

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:43.800
Days of Future Past, played by Evan Peters.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.020
"You didn't see that coming?"

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:52.320
Not according to Marvel Studios President
Kevin Feige, who in 2015 told MTV that Quicksilver

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.570
died to elevate the stakes of Age of Ultron,
and more importantly to guide the future of

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:58.940
his sister Wanda, played by Elizabeth Olsen.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.060
Feige told MTV the speedster's death acted
to

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.510
"...solidify Scarlet Witch's character, and
Wanda's arc in the movie and where we'll see

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:06.909
her in the next films."

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:10.619
If Quicksilver had lived, he maybe would've
had a thing or two to say about his sister

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.540
getting into a relationship with an android.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:16.329
Whichever side Quicksilver would've chosen
in Captain America: Civil War would've likely

00:02:16.329 --> 00:02:17.780
impacted Wanda's choices.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.920
She may not have automatically sided with
him, but Quicksilver's support or lack thereof

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.019
could've affected her decision.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:26.940
By the time Infinity War rolls around, it's
safe to assume that the Scarlet Witch we're

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.970
left with is one who is much more independent.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:29.500
All the "decimated"

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.480
What exactly happened to the planet Xandar?

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:37.150
In Avengers: Infinity War, Thor explains to
the Guardians how Thanos and his forces got

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.150
the Power Stone:

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:41.230
"There are six stones out there.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:46.260
Thanos already has the power stone because
he stole it last week when he decimated Xandar."

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.580
"Decimated" is a powerful word, but not a
specific one.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.560
Did he literally kill everyone on the planet?

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.560
Or 10% of the planet for all you "that's not
what decimation means!" people.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.640
You know who you are....

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:01.769
One tantalizing possibility: We're going to
see Xandar transformed in one of Marvel's

00:03:01.769 --> 00:03:02.640
upcoming movies.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.840
We may even see its Nova Corps grow closer
to the source material.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:09.720
In Guardians of the Galaxy, the Nova Corps
is made up of relatively normal people..

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:13.909
In the comics, it's a different story: every
member of the Corps has super powers.

00:03:13.909 --> 00:03:16.590
They're essentially Marvel's answer to the
Green Lantern Corps.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:19.120
Instead of rings, they're given helmets that
grant them powers.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.980
Their abilities aren't nearly as versatile
as the Lanterns', but at the same time they’re

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:25.360
a whole lot less CGI then them as well.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.620
"Ahh Green!"

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.799
If Xandar survived after weathering two separate
assaults by alien maniacs, its inhabitants

00:03:34.799 --> 00:03:38.749
may decide it's about time they build an army
capable of more than just piloting spaceships

00:03:38.749 --> 00:03:39.760
and arresting raccoons.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.820
They might do whatever it takes to found the
real Nova Corps.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.720
Kurt Russell's Ego identifies as a Celestial
before his defeat at the end of Guardians

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.100
of the Galaxy Volume 2.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.100
This race of mysterious beings has nearly
limitless power.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.960
In the comics, they even hold the keys to
many of the universe's biggest mysteries.

00:03:55.969 --> 00:04:00.469
That's one of many ways Ego differs from his
comic book counterpart, who is literally a

00:04:00.469 --> 00:04:01.860
planet with a giant planet-sized face.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:05.060
But that's not the part that's particularly
meaningful about his death.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:08.979
Instead, it points towards one of the MCU
franchises we haven't seen yet.

00:04:08.979 --> 00:04:13.760
We know Marvel Studios is gearing up to introduce
audiences to the Eternals, a race of superhumans

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:16.730
whose origins are very much intertwined with
the Celestials.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:20.500
In the comics, the Celestials created the
Eternals specifically to defend the Earth

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.510
against their opposite the Deviants.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:25.880
If the movie characters remains true to the
comics, it's likely we'll be learning way

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:29.820
more about the Celestials than we ever did
in Guardians of the Galaxy or any other Marvel

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:30.860
Studios films.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:34.900
The fact that Ego was killed by an Earthman
could be of great interest to Marvel's newest

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:35.400
heroes.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:39.540
"You shouldn’t have killed my mom and squished
my Walkman."

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:43.480
He evidently believed he was the only Celestial
in existence.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.140
In Captain America: The Winter Soldier, we
learn that Arnim Zola died years before while

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:52.340
secretly working with the freshly resurrected
terrorist organization Hydra.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:53.680
"Hail Hydra."

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:58.220
But Zola also sneakily transcribed his memories
and personality into data.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:02.410
The result is an exposition scene outlining
what Hydra had been up to for 70 years.

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:05.930
It's also a clever visual tribute to the Arnim
Zola of the comics.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:10.840
Curiously, there's something that's been left
completely unsaid in the MCU so far: For Hydra,

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:15.530
Arnim Zola Artificial Intelligence had to
have been an important step down a very specific

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:16.020
road.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:19.960
In Avengers: Age of Ultron, we learn a piece
of vital information during a conversation

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:23.850
between Bruce Banner and Tony Stark about
the possibility of finally realizing their

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:28.220
Ultron project, Stark says his research on
the scepter leads him to believe Hydra was

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.240
using it to develop an advanced artificial
intelligence.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.380
"Artificial intelligence."

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.420
"This could be it, Bruce.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.120
This could be the key to creating Ultron."

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:44.820
If Stark is correct, then the creation of
the Zola A.I. must have been part of the research

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.680
that ultimately leads to the birth of Ultron
and Vision.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:51.640
In fact, fans almost saw some persuasive evidence
to back up this theory.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:56.740
In November 2016, some concept art from Ant-Man
leaked, and it revealed that director Peyton

00:05:56.740 --> 00:06:01.341
Reed considered bringing Zola back for the
prologue scene at the SHIELD Triskelion, still

00:06:01.341 --> 00:06:02.260
under construction.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:06.300
Since Ant-Man was the first film to follow
Age of Ultron, it might have helped cement

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.100
the notion that Zola was, in fact, Ultron's
ancestor.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:15.140
In Iron Man 2, Mickey Rourke's character Ivan
Vanko , also known as Whiplash, swears vengeance

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.120
on Tony Stark.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:20.580
That's because Ivan was taught that Stark's
father Howard stole the idea for the game-changing

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.120
Arc Reactor from his father.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:26.480
Twice in the film, we see a small bit of evidence
that seems to support this: design schematics

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:28.900
with Vanko's name listed before Stark's.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:33.020
Nick Fury employs an interesting strategy
when trying to rein in Stark's crazy behavior:

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:36.830
He tells Stark that Vanko was full of it,
insisting that all of his claims of stolen

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.460
innovation could be chalked up to his anger
after being shipped off to Siberia.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:43.460
"He spent the next 20 years in a vodka-fuelled
rage."

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:48.580
But we never definitively learn whether Whiplash's
father's accusations were valid.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.620
Fury says they weren't.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:54.300
In The Avengers, Fury also says that SHIELD
is only interested in the Tesseract because

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.220
of the clean energy it can provide, and that's
a big fat lie.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.340
Fury is far from a reliable source.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:03.440
It is curious that Vanko's name came first
on the schematics both on the copies Vanko

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:07.060
has early in the film and the one Stark finds
in the stuff S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:08.200
brings him from storage.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:11.250
Regardless, we'll probably never get to the
bottom of this one.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:12.340
Whiplash certainly didn't.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:16.540
In Doctor Strange, the death of the Ancient
One raises questions that aren't answered

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:17.560
by the end of the film.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:21.800
And even though Stephen Strange appears in
Thor: Ragnarok and Avengers: Infinity War,

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:23.860
those questions still have yet to be answered.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:26.700
There are hints, perhaps, but nothing concrete
yet.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.260
You know what we're getting at here.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:31.020
Basically, what exactly happened to Kamar-Taj?

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:39.760
Immediately after the Ancient One's death,
Strange and Mordo head to Hong Kong.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:44.550
By the end of the film, The Ancient One's
death leaves a huge void in Kamar-taj's leadership

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:48.200
and we have no idea who, if anyone, has stepped
up to fill it.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.490
When you think about it, The Ancient One and
her students are apparently the only ones

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.770
standing between the MCU's Earth and hordes
of malevolent forces.

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:58.430
So honestly, the question of who's steering
the ship now that she's gone seems like a

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:00.510
pretty important one to answer straight away.

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:05.020
One of the hints we get is Doctor Strange's
conspicuous leap in terms of his mystic skills.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.980
In Doctor Strange, he can barely keep up with
Kaecilius's henchmen.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:11.880
But by Infinity War, the guy gives Thanos
a better one-on-one fight than just about

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:15.720
any other hero in the movie, and that's when
Thanos has four Infinity Stones.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:19.800
Could it be possible that Strange was allowed
to assume leadership of Kamar-taj in spite

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.140
of being the new kid on the block?

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:22.540
"It's Strange."

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.020
"Maybe.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.880
Who am I to judge?"

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:29.900
Discuss amongst yourselves.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:34.180
Want to know our vote for the most surprising
death in 2018's Black Panther?

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:38.000
It had to be when Killmonger, played by Michael
B. Jordan, kills Ulysses Klaue.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.340
"And to think I saw you as some crazy American."

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:50.420
Initially introduced as a weapons dealer in
the 2015 film Avengers: Age of Ultron, some

00:08:50.431 --> 00:08:54.579
fans thought Klaue might be the main villain
of Black Panther, and for very good reason.

00:08:54.579 --> 00:08:59.059
For quite a while, Ulysses Klaw has not only
been the Wakandan monarch's most persistent

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:01.240
foe, he was actually T'Challa's first enemy.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:05.620
In the comics, Ulysses Klaue is much more
than a thief to Wakanda: He's the killer of

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:06.120
a king.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:10.500
While trying to steal Wakanda's vibranium
for himself, it's Ulysses who murders T'Challa's

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:11.560
father T'Chaka.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:15.740
Still just a boy, T'Challa shoots Ulysses
with his own sonic weapon, causing him to

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:19.769
be transformed into the villain Klaw, a being
composed of solidified sound.

00:09:19.769 --> 00:09:23.000
Black Panther director Ryan Coogler didn't
like killing off Klaue.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.220
In May 2018, he told the Toronto Sun:

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:26.230
"I like Klaw.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:27.970
It really bugged me having to [kill him].

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:31.440
It's tough when you have to kill characters
off and I really did love that character."

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:32.500
"I'm sorry.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.180
I'm so.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:34.180
Ohhhh…

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.740
I'm sure that's gonna be okay.

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:36.240
I'm sorry.”

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:41.160
Considering Coogler's fondness for both Klaw
and actor Andy Serkis, could we one day see

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:44.579
Klaue return as a villain that's a little
closer to the source material?

00:09:44.579 --> 00:09:48.149
It seems quite possible, especially considering
it looks like Coogler might be willing to

00:09:48.149 --> 00:09:51.360
resurrect a certain special someone for Black
Panther 2.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.700
"Just so I could kill you."

